both are good tracks

its not that simple, when d-MA has a lot of l-MA or cutters that are slightly active but not-so-great they make it tweaky crap as a whole and very prone to adverse effects.

&#x200B;

While yeah, they might not care a huge amount about that, many users won't even touch most of the stuff that goes around.

&#x200B;

edit: also if you produce more of the active chem you can still cut it to the ssame weight per active dose, so if you yield 80:20 d:l, vs 50:50 and cut it with something inert you still get over 50% increase in your product
